WEBVTT

00:02.633 --> 00:05.863
<i>It seems today that all you see</i>

00:05.970 --> 00:09.236
<i>Is violence in movies and sex on TV</i>

00:09.341 --> 00:12.605
<i>But where are those
good old-fashioned values</i>

00:12.710 --> 00:15.610
<i>On which we used to rely?</i>

00:16.079 --> 00:19.311
<i>Lucky there's a family guy</i>

00:19.416 --> 00:22.409
<i>Lucky there's a man who
Positively can do</i>

00:22.520 --> 00:24.179
<i>All the things that make us</i>

00:24.287 --> 00:25.812
<i>Laugh and cry</i>

00:26.056 --> 00:30.858
<i>He's a family guy</i>

00:38.134 --> 00:41.467
Oh, yes! I slam it, and you can suck it!

00:41.571 --> 00:43.834
Joe, that was our last ball.

00:43.940 --> 00:45.907
Don't worry. Mr. Moose will help us out.

00:46.008 --> 00:48.533
- Won't you, Mr. Moose?
- Fine.

00:48.644 --> 00:50.908
- Knock-knock.
- Ping pong balls!

00:53.882 --> 00:56.146
Hey, guys, look at me. I'm covered in balls.

00:56.250 --> 00:57.514
- Just like...
- Just like Sharon Stone.

00:57.619 --> 00:58.745
You beat me to it.

00:58.854 --> 01:01.948
Man, I haven't had this much fun
since I was in that Broadway show.

01:05.828 --> 01:11.322
<i>I'm a Wolverine
And my hatred keeps me warm</i>

01:11.431 --> 01:17.098
<i>A wolverine
So you Russians best be warned</i>

01:17.205 --> 01:18.604
<i>Shooting commies
Drinking deer blood</i>

01:18.706 --> 01:20.765
<i>Peeing in the radiator
Look up there</i>

01:20.875 --> 01:23.275
<i>Here comes a really
Angry Russian helicopter</i>

01:27.748 --> 01:31.310
It has been a red dawn.

01:31.819 --> 01:34.913
Hey, Peter, Lois called to remind you
to pick up Meg at the roller rink.

01:35.023 --> 01:36.581
- No!
- We're just getting started!

01:36.691 --> 01:39.420
Meg is my least favorite
of all your children.

01:39.527 --> 01:41.961
It's all right. We'll just move the party
to the skating rink.

01:42.063 --> 01:43.756
Who's sober enough to drive?

01:44.766 --> 01:47.325
Okay, who's drunk,
but that special kind of drunk

01:47.434 --> 01:49.595
where you're a better driver
because you know you're drunk?

01:49.704 --> 01:51.761
You know, the kind of drunk
where you probably shouldn't drive,

01:51.872 --> 01:53.169
but you do anyway because,

01:53.273 --> 01:55.537
I mean, come on,
you gotta get your car home, right?

01:55.642 --> 01:58.132
I mean, what do they expect me to do,
take a bus?

01:58.244 --> 02:00.770
Is that what they want,
for me to take a bus?

02:00.881 --> 02:03.975
Well, screw that. You take a bus.

02:04.083 --> 02:06.449
- I'm that kind of drunk.
- Shotgun.

02:12.124 --> 02:15.251
Dad, where have you been?
I've been waiting for over an hour.

02:15.361 --> 02:18.023
Grab some wood there, bub.
Daddy and his friends have been drinking,

02:18.131 --> 02:21.123
and we're gonna keep on drinking
until we each uncover repressed memories

02:21.233 --> 02:23.996
of sexual abuse
by a trusted religious official.

02:24.103 --> 02:29.336
Oh, that's crazy talk. Oh, my God!
Minister Washington, how could you?

02:29.442 --> 02:31.204
Man, look at all these chicks.

02:33.211 --> 02:34.201
If I were a woman,

02:34.313 --> 02:37.407
I would press my bare boobs
up against glass in public

02:37.516 --> 02:42.385
just for the sexual thrill! The sexual thrill!

02:43.888 --> 02:47.086
- How do I stop?
- Use the rubber stoppers on the front.

02:49.060 --> 02:51.619
Hey, baby, how'd you like
to share a pair of skates?

02:51.728 --> 02:53.889
- Sure!
- Never mind!

02:53.997 --> 02:57.229
- Boy, you look a lot better from the back.
- You jerk!

02:57.334 --> 02:59.461
Oh, hey, baby,
you want to go somewhere?

02:59.570 --> 03:03.029
No, no, no! Wait. Wait. Quagmire,
remember what's on the other side.

03:34.538 --> 03:35.526
That was awesome!

03:35.638 --> 03:38.072
Oh, my God!
That was completely by accident.

03:38.174 --> 03:39.141
That was great fun.

03:39.241 --> 03:41.437
I don't even remember why we came,
but I had a ball.

03:41.545 --> 03:43.569
I look forward to reminiscing
about this tomorrow.

03:44.646 --> 03:47.707
Dad! Wait! You forgot me again!

03:48.451 --> 03:50.477
You need a lift?
Didn't answer me quick enough.

03:59.529 --> 04:02.191
<i>Remember those sweet,
warm New England summers?</i>

04:02.464 --> 04:05.524
<i>Remember sipping lemonade
underneath a shady tree?</i>

04:05.635 --> 04:08.730
<i>Remember when you hit that pedestrian
with your car at the crosswalk</i>

04:08.838 --> 04:10.532
<i>and then just drove away?</i>

04:10.639 --> 04:12.470
<i>Pepperidge Farm remembers.</i>

04:12.574 --> 04:14.099
<i>But Pepperidge Farm
ain't just gonna keep it</i>

04:14.208 --> 04:16.335
<i>to Pepperidge Farm's self free of charge.</i>

04:16.443 --> 04:19.437
<i>Maybe you go out and buy yourself
some of these distinctive Milano cookies.</i>

04:19.548 --> 04:21.515
<i>Maybe this whole thing just disappears.</i>

04:22.051 --> 04:23.676
Meg, what happened?

04:23.784 --> 04:26.719
Fat-ass and his drunk friends left me
at the roller rink.

04:26.821 --> 04:29.414
You know, this wouldn't have happened
if I had my own car.

04:29.523 --> 04:32.493
Meg, people have always found ways
to get around without a car.

04:32.594 --> 04:33.617
Look at Iceman.

04:35.197 --> 04:37.097
Honey, where'd you go
when you went out last night?

04:37.464 --> 04:38.726
Just over to Tom's house.

04:38.832 --> 04:40.858
Played some poker, had some brewskis.
You know.

04:40.969 --> 04:43.732
Really?
Then would you mind explaining that?

04:48.076 --> 04:52.170
At least they know how to touch a man.
Oh, walk away.

04:52.278 --> 04:55.679
You know, Peter, maybe Meg
having her own car isn't such a bad idea.

04:55.782 --> 04:58.080
- Yeah, I guess so.
- What?

04:58.184 --> 05:00.618
I have been trying
to get a sewing machine for months,

05:00.720 --> 05:03.153
but she gets a freaking car just like that!

05:03.255 --> 05:04.554
I hate this place.

05:07.361 --> 05:08.588
Look at all these Hummers.

05:08.695 --> 05:10.663
What kind of jerk
would drive one of those?

05:12.165 --> 05:13.757
Dude, this car kicks ass,

05:13.866 --> 05:16.834
<i>and I can watch Madagascar
while I'm driving!</i>

05:17.271 --> 05:22.069
<i>- What kind of music do you like, Gloria?
- Hippo-hop. Woohoo! Yeah, baby!</i>

05:23.177 --> 05:25.644
Dude, those animals are so fucking funny,

05:25.745 --> 05:27.804
they make me want to merge
without looking!

05:30.215 --> 05:32.081
Yeah! Rumsfeld!

05:32.184 --> 05:33.743
Hi, there, can I help you folks?

05:33.852 --> 05:36.844
Yeah, my daughter's looking for a car
that goes with her personality.

05:36.955 --> 05:39.752
Yes, are the new bulimic-cutting mobiles
in yet?

05:39.857 --> 05:41.689
This is a 1996 sedan.

05:41.793 --> 05:44.887
Excellent gas mileage, air bags
and AM-FM cassette.

05:44.997 --> 05:49.057
- I love it! Dad, this is the car.
- Hang on a second, Meg.

05:49.166 --> 05:50.395
What can you tell me about this one?

05:50.502 --> 05:52.901
Oh, that's just an old tank I use
for those commercials

05:53.004 --> 05:55.097
where I declare war on high prices.

05:55.206 --> 05:56.731
Now, about that sedan...

05:57.275 --> 05:59.710
Hang on there, slick. Now I see your game.

05:59.811 --> 06:01.641
We come in here wanting a practical car,

06:01.746 --> 06:03.373
but then you dangle this tank
in front of me

06:03.481 --> 06:04.812
and expect me to walk away.

06:04.915 --> 06:08.008
Now, I may be an idiot,
but there is one thing I am not, sir,

06:08.118 --> 06:09.950
and that, sir, is an idiot.

06:10.054 --> 06:12.455
Now, I demand
you tell me more about this tank.

06:15.525 --> 06:17.687
Well, if you're looking for quality,
then look no further.

06:17.796 --> 06:20.592
That's more like it. Tell me,
what are the tank's safety features?

06:20.697 --> 06:22.164
What a good-looking question.

06:22.266 --> 06:24.961
Three inches of reinforced steel
protects your daughter

06:25.068 --> 06:26.432
from short-range missile attacks.

06:26.535 --> 06:28.937
I see, and does the sedan protect
against missiles?

06:29.039 --> 06:31.007
- It does not.
- You hear that, Meg?

06:31.108 --> 06:32.870
Yeah, it does not protect against missiles.

06:32.975 --> 06:35.637
See, these are the questions.
This is why I'm here.

06:35.744 --> 06:38.908
Peter, you can't be serious.
This is a 30-ton war machine.

06:39.015 --> 06:40.914
I'm still not sure.

06:41.016 --> 06:43.109
- Did I mention the tank is a tank?
- Sold.

06:45.520 --> 06:48.183
Okay, Lois, you can open your eyes.

06:48.290 --> 06:50.918
- Bocce balls!
- I bought a tank.

06:51.026 --> 06:52.358
Are you out of your mind?

06:52.462 --> 06:53.792
Let me show you how the gun works.

06:59.467 --> 07:00.991
What the hell?

07:01.103 --> 07:04.834
No, no, no, no!

07:05.207 --> 07:08.142
Hey, Peter, can you blow
that towel rack down here?

07:09.510 --> 07:10.739
Thank you.

07:12.546 --> 07:18.111
<i>Jeff Daniels and Bill Pullman
star in Neil Simon's The Even Couple.</i>

07:18.519 --> 07:21.682
- I ordered a pizza. I hope that's okay.
- Sure, I love pizza.

07:22.323 --> 07:23.757
This half of the apartment is mine,

07:23.859 --> 07:25.986
but if you want to come over here,
that's okay, too.

07:26.095 --> 07:27.652
This isn't spaghetti. It's linguini.

07:27.762 --> 07:30.458
You're right. It is.
I always get those confused.

07:30.564 --> 07:32.693
- Hey, all of us are human.
- I'm glad we're friends.

07:32.801 --> 07:34.132
Yeah, this is really working out.

07:34.235 --> 07:36.669
There's no conflict in this movie!

07:37.739 --> 07:39.569
When are you gonna get rid of that stump?

07:39.673 --> 07:42.074
I've been asking you for months
to get rid of that stump!

07:42.176 --> 07:44.166
I'll do it, all right? Just get off my back!

07:47.981 --> 07:50.643
She's gone. We can finally be together.

07:50.752 --> 07:52.651
But, Tim, I'm rooted the ground.

07:52.753 --> 07:55.489
We'll find a way. We'll find a way.

07:58.925 --> 08:02.622
My God, it's hot.
Brian, did you turn off the air conditioner?

08:02.729 --> 08:05.596
Just open a window. Air conditioners
are harmful to the ozone layer.

08:05.965 --> 08:09.265
Brian, please, save your hippie BS
for the winter months, okay?

08:09.369 --> 08:11.734
Hey, Brian,
I'm not gonna recycle this aluminum can.

08:11.837 --> 08:13.500
I'm just gonna throw it in the trash.

08:22.148 --> 08:24.049
Your Earth's bitch.

08:24.150 --> 08:27.141
Morning, civilians.
General Griffin reporting for breakfast.

08:27.253 --> 08:28.721
Dad, it's not fair.

08:28.821 --> 08:32.188
My money paid for that tank,
and I haven't even got to drive it yet.

08:32.291 --> 08:34.657
Jeez, Meg,
you always gotta ruin my good time,

08:34.760 --> 08:35.885
just like basic cable.

08:36.227 --> 08:37.786
<i>We now return to Showgirls...</i>

08:37.897 --> 08:38.921
Yeah!

08:39.031 --> 08:40.123
<i>...on TBS.</i>

08:42.768 --> 08:46.100
All right, Meg, you got a feel
for the controls. Now give it a little gas.

08:49.941 --> 08:52.877
Oh, great, it's here.
That mirror I bought on eBay.

08:53.745 --> 08:54.870
Oh, my God!

08:58.951 --> 09:00.975
Joe, my God, what happened?

09:01.085 --> 09:03.211
You just ran over me, you bastard!

09:03.321 --> 09:06.518
I don't know where you got that thing,
but I'm impounding it!

09:07.459 --> 09:10.120
Look at you.
You look like a half-empty toothpaste.

09:14.365 --> 09:16.855
<i>We now return
to the Ghost Whisperer.</i>

09:16.968 --> 09:19.937
<i>I don't understand.
Why do all you ghosts come to me?</i>

09:20.037 --> 09:22.232
<i>You're really...
I mean, you have a knack for...</i>

09:22.339 --> 09:23.829
<i>We just trust you.</i>

09:23.941 --> 09:28.537
I can't believe you let Mr. Swanson
confiscate the closest thing I had to a car.

09:28.645 --> 09:31.079
Relax, Meg.
It's not the worst thing I've ever done.

09:31.181 --> 09:33.615
You remember that favor I did
for that park ranger?

09:33.717 --> 09:36.652
Hey, Boo Boo, let's see
what we got in this pic-a-nic basket.

09:43.660 --> 09:45.889
Tell the other bears what you just saw.

09:46.263 --> 09:47.251
Well, I don't care

09:47.363 --> 09:51.026
'cause you know what I'm gonna do?
I'm gonna get a job and buy a real car.

09:51.133 --> 09:55.069
Hey, Meg, I'll pay you a dollar a day
to smell my sneakers.

10:14.189 --> 10:15.486
I peed and pooped.

10:15.590 --> 10:19.152
You know, I read that they're opening
a Superstore USA across town.

10:19.261 --> 10:20.558
Maybe you could get a job there.

10:20.662 --> 10:22.687
No. No, no way.
You cannot work there, Meg.

10:22.797 --> 10:26.197
Giant megastores like Superstore USA
are ruining this country.

10:26.300 --> 10:28.098
They don't pay their employees
a decent wage

10:28.203 --> 10:29.226
or give them health benefits.

10:29.337 --> 10:31.770
- Yeah, all gay guys hate Superstore USA.
- What?

10:32.207 --> 10:33.503
Hey, I'm just trying to be ethical.

10:33.607 --> 10:37.133
Yeah, right. You hate all megastores
ever since you were petted way too hard

10:37.244 --> 10:39.337
by that special boy in front of Kmart.

10:41.049 --> 10:42.709
Doggie!

10:42.816 --> 10:44.114
Doggie!

10:44.217 --> 10:45.616
- Doggie!
- Too hard.

10:45.718 --> 10:47.619
- I like doggie!
- Too hard.

10:47.721 --> 10:49.155
- Doggie!
- Gonna bite.

10:49.257 --> 10:50.847
- Doggie!
- Gonna bite.

10:50.957 --> 10:52.186
Doggie!

10:55.494 --> 10:56.895
Oh, jeez.

11:03.302 --> 11:05.931
Welcome to the Superstore family, Meg.
Glad to have you.

11:06.039 --> 11:08.167
Thanks. I'm really excited to get to work.

11:08.275 --> 11:10.209
Now, let me just go over a few basics.

11:10.311 --> 11:13.040
You'll earn minimum wage,
no overtime, no health benefits,

11:13.146 --> 11:16.912
and every day at 3:00,
you'll need to give Sloth a Baby Ruth.

11:17.016 --> 11:18.847
Oh, it's nearly 3:00 now.

11:22.220 --> 11:25.486
- Here you go.
- You're beautiful.

11:25.593 --> 11:30.585
I would go out with you if I wasn't already
in a committed relationship.

11:40.038 --> 11:41.266
Hey, guys, what's going on?

11:41.406 --> 11:45.240
Oh, Peter, Superstore USA
has taken all my business.

11:45.345 --> 11:48.903
Mine, too. In fact, the only guy in town
making any money

11:49.014 --> 11:51.346
is that guy who makes tumbleweeds.

11:51.449 --> 11:56.182
Y'all laughed at me. Y'all laughed at me.
Well, who's laughing now?

11:58.423 --> 11:59.514
What do you think of this?

11:59.624 --> 12:02.491
- That makes you attractive.
- Yeah!

12:03.961 --> 12:06.759
Well, maybe now you guys are seeing
what I've been trying to explain to you.

12:06.864 --> 12:09.195
That megastore is a big, evil corporation

12:09.299 --> 12:11.063
that means nothing but trouble
for this town.

12:11.168 --> 12:13.329
Oh, man, this is the worst thing
to happen to this town

12:13.437 --> 12:15.962
since that roving gang of Tom Brokaws.

12:19.944 --> 12:22.606
Looks like someone's a little lost.

12:24.782 --> 12:26.907
Everyone, I have some bad news.

12:27.017 --> 12:29.611
Superstore USA
has their own brewery on site

12:29.719 --> 12:31.949
and can sell beer at a much cheaper price,

12:32.056 --> 12:34.354
so management has decided
to close down.

12:34.458 --> 12:37.290
- You mean I'm out of a job again?
- I'm sorry, Peter.

12:37.393 --> 12:40.794
Man, this sucks worse than Easter Sunday
at Richard Gere's house.

12:41.031 --> 12:42.827
Okay, find the Easter egg.

12:42.931 --> 12:46.367
- I know where it is. It's in your butt.
- No.

12:46.468 --> 12:48.994
Yeah, I know the story. It's in your butt.

12:49.105 --> 12:52.905
Mr. Griffin, if you'd just look on the ground
for five seconds, I'm sure you'd find it.

12:53.009 --> 12:55.443
- Nope, in your butt.
- Look, I'm tired of this stupid rumor.

12:55.545 --> 12:56.602
- In your butt.
- Mr. Griffin...

12:56.712 --> 12:57.681
- Butt. Butt.
- Mr. Griffin...

12:57.781 --> 12:59.645
You know what?
Just get the hell out of here.

12:59.747 --> 13:01.375
Fine. Weirdo.

13:07.655 --> 13:09.420
So how was work today, Meg?

13:09.525 --> 13:12.288
Peter, you lost your job
because of the Superstore.

13:12.393 --> 13:13.918
You shouldn't blame Meg.

13:14.029 --> 13:17.397
And you can stop making that fart sound
every time someone says, "Meg. "

13:17.765 --> 13:20.700
So how was your day
exploiting the town's resources, Meg?

13:22.303 --> 13:23.270
Meg.

13:23.670 --> 13:25.071
Meg.

13:26.375 --> 13:28.864
Meg, Meg, Meg, Meg, Meg, Meg!

13:31.144 --> 13:32.112
Meg.

13:33.648 --> 13:35.377
I'm not gonna sit here and take this.

13:35.483 --> 13:37.917
I'm the only one in this family
who has a job.

13:38.619 --> 13:40.052
Yeah, like she'd get paid for that.

13:40.154 --> 13:42.714
- What did he just say to you?
- Nothing, there was...

13:43.092 --> 13:46.254
Well, it's like if you were...
Forget it. It's nothing, Meg.

13:49.564 --> 13:51.896
<i>- Hello, I'm Tom Tucker.
- And I'm Diane Simmons.</i>

13:51.999 --> 13:55.526
<i>At the top of the news, Quahog is
suffering its worst heat wave in a century.</i>

13:55.635 --> 13:57.899
<i>That's right, Diane.
We now go live to Ollie Williams</i>

13:58.004 --> 14:00.472
<i>with the black-you weather report.
How are you beating the heat, Ollie?</i>

14:00.574 --> 14:02.042
<i>- Swimming hole!
- Thanks, Ollie.</i>

14:02.143 --> 14:05.009
<i>In other news, Quahog
will be experiencing rolling blackouts</i>

14:05.112 --> 14:08.205
<i>to help meet Superstore USA's
extensive power demands.</i>

14:08.314 --> 14:12.842
<i>Oh, in fact, Channel Five has just received
this message from the Electric Company.</i>

14:12.953 --> 14:16.183
<i>Hey, you guys!</i>

14:18.057 --> 14:20.959
<i>We're gonna turn it on</i>

14:21.061 --> 14:24.188
<i>We're gonna bring you the power</i>

14:24.297 --> 14:27.629
<i>It's coming down the line
Strong as it can be</i>

14:27.733 --> 14:33.535
<i>Through the courtesy
Of the Electric Company</i>

14:38.577 --> 14:39.873
<i>Contrary to those upbeat lyrics,</i>

14:39.979 --> 14:41.673
<i>the Electric Company
would like us to emphasize</i>

14:41.780 --> 14:43.373
<i>it will not be bringing you the power.</i>

14:44.716 --> 14:46.207
Great, rolling blackouts.

14:46.316 --> 14:49.343
Now, Superstore USA
is siphoning off all the city's power.

14:49.455 --> 14:51.979
- And they cost me my job.
- Mine, too.

14:52.090 --> 14:54.990
Superstore USA
has their own paper route.

14:58.730 --> 15:02.166
That new paperboy done gone
and broke my sternum.

15:16.680 --> 15:19.650
This sucks. That damn Superstore
is ruining everything.

15:19.751 --> 15:21.307
You know,
instead of sitting around complaining,

15:21.417 --> 15:23.147
why don't we go down there and protest?

15:23.253 --> 15:24.686
That's a great idea, Brian.

15:24.789 --> 15:27.814
All we need is some magic markers,
poster boards, some plywood...

15:27.925 --> 15:30.794
Actually, Superstore USA
has all that stuff. We can just get it there.

15:41.371 --> 15:42.632
There's one of them now.

15:42.738 --> 15:45.467
Take that for stealing jobs
from hardworking people!

15:47.277 --> 15:49.210
Dad, what the hell are you doing?

15:49.312 --> 15:53.476
We got a message for you.
"We're here. We're queer. Get used to it. "

15:53.582 --> 15:56.210
<i>- Actually, Peter...
- Gattaca! Gattaca!</i>

15:56.319 --> 15:58.981
Peter, I don't think it's working.
People are still going into the store.

16:01.190 --> 16:04.819
Well, fine, then I guess I gotta go in there
and drag them out one by one.

16:07.596 --> 16:09.393
All right, who the hell is in charge...

16:10.497 --> 16:12.729
What is that I'm feeling?

16:12.835 --> 16:14.929
That's our industrial-sized air conditioner.

16:15.804 --> 16:19.296
When I walk into Superstore USA,
I get the sensation

16:19.407 --> 16:23.969
that I'm standing on a mountain top
with the wind blowing through my hair!

16:24.079 --> 16:27.536
My God,
look at this wonderland of treasures.

16:27.648 --> 16:31.244
What would a guy like me have to do
to be part of this magical world?

16:31.585 --> 16:35.112
You are trespassing on private property,
and I must ask you to leave.

16:35.222 --> 16:37.122
What? Are you out of your mind?

16:37.625 --> 16:40.958
- Leave this lot, losers.
- Unless you want a licking.

16:41.062 --> 16:43.120
And we'd love to deliver that licking,

16:43.230 --> 16:44.198
- right, fellows?
- Yeah.

16:44.299 --> 16:45.286
- Love it.
- A lot.

16:45.398 --> 16:48.927
I'd love to lick a lemon lollipop
in Lillehammer.

16:55.376 --> 16:57.504
God, I wish the power
would come back on.

16:57.612 --> 17:00.011
Boy, Meg, I am so looking forward
to this job.

17:00.114 --> 17:02.514
Peter, I can't believe
you're working for Superstore USA.

17:02.616 --> 17:04.207
How could you sell out like that?

17:04.317 --> 17:07.446
Because, Brian, they have
an industrial-sized air conditioner,

17:07.555 --> 17:09.521
and I'm tired of sitting in ball soup.

17:09.621 --> 17:11.920
Look, Dad,
this isn't gonna be a cake walk, all right?

17:12.025 --> 17:13.185
I'm your supervisor.

17:13.293 --> 17:16.821
Meg. Meg, I promise, I'll do better
at this job than I did on the SATs.

17:24.404 --> 17:27.306
Come on, do math.

17:29.876 --> 17:33.106
Dad, I need you to...
Dad, what are you doing?

17:33.344 --> 17:36.804
Meg. Meg, look. Meg, look.
I am so freaking good at coloring.

17:36.916 --> 17:38.883
I know I'm not supposed
to go outside the lines,

17:38.985 --> 17:41.247
but I do anyway
because I like being myself.

17:43.656 --> 17:44.713
Dad?

17:47.659 --> 17:48.717
Dad?

17:50.963 --> 17:51.985
Dad?

17:59.203 --> 18:01.501
Oh, God, it's so hot.

18:01.605 --> 18:04.074
Brian, spit on me.

18:04.543 --> 18:07.842
Oh, that's nice. Now tell me I'm scum.

18:07.946 --> 18:09.207
How will that cool you off?

18:10.113 --> 18:11.946
God, it's awful in here.

18:12.050 --> 18:14.950
This is even worse than getting herpes
from a toilet seat.

18:15.052 --> 18:17.111
Joanie, it's me.

18:17.221 --> 18:21.181
Oh, hey! You know, I had
such a great time with you last night.

18:21.293 --> 18:23.625
Listen, there's something
I have to tell you.

18:23.729 --> 18:26.788
I just got back from the doctor.
I have herpes.

18:26.896 --> 18:28.488
I think you should
get yourself checked out.

18:28.597 --> 18:29.623
Oh, my God.

18:29.734 --> 18:31.497
- Will you stay?
- What?

18:31.603 --> 18:34.537
Will you stay with me
even knowing that I have herpes?

18:35.538 --> 18:37.301
Yes, I will.

18:37.640 --> 18:39.130
- Joanie?
- Yeah?

18:39.376 --> 18:42.778
I don't have herpes.
I just needed to know that you'd stay.

18:49.486 --> 18:52.580
I've had it. The only place in town
that's got power is Superstore USA

18:52.689 --> 18:54.917
while the rest of us
are left to bake in the heat.

18:55.024 --> 18:57.391
There's gotta be something we can do
to take that place down.

18:57.493 --> 19:00.588
Don't worry, Brian. I think I've got an idea.

19:02.964 --> 19:04.262
Uh-huh.

19:04.366 --> 19:05.925
Oh, yeah!

19:09.873 --> 19:12.272
Excuse me, can you tell me
where I can find assault rifles?

19:12.374 --> 19:13.362
Aisle six.

19:13.474 --> 19:15.533
How about a list
of known local homosexuals?

19:15.643 --> 19:16.633
Aisle four.

19:16.745 --> 19:18.644
Meg, you're doing a great job.

19:18.746 --> 19:21.682
In fact, I'm promoting you
to assistant manager.

19:21.784 --> 19:25.049
Really? Oh, my God! Thank you so much.

19:25.153 --> 19:29.282
Now, your first responsibility
is to fire that employee.

19:29.391 --> 19:32.224
Boy, I'm a little chilly.
I hope no one notices.

19:35.531 --> 19:36.554
But that's my dad.

19:36.665 --> 19:39.326
What's more important to you,
your job or your family?

19:39.566 --> 19:40.931
And don't pick the obvious one.

19:41.035 --> 19:43.594
Oh, hey, guys. I was just catching up
on some plunger nipples.

19:43.704 --> 19:44.830
Dad...

19:45.506 --> 19:47.940
Go on, Meg. What are you waiting for?

19:53.314 --> 19:55.406
Dad, I'm sorry I have to say this,

19:55.515 --> 19:57.642
but you're a fat-ass

19:57.751 --> 20:01.187
who's completely incapable
of performing the simplest tasks,

20:01.888 --> 20:04.652
but you're also my father,

20:05.092 --> 20:07.492
and you're the only one I'll ever have,

20:07.927 --> 20:10.623
so I'm not going to fire you.

20:11.098 --> 20:13.259
Mr. Penisberg, I quit.

20:13.366 --> 20:17.358
- Penisberg?
- Yeah, yeah, get it all out of your system.

20:17.470 --> 20:20.496
Meg, that was a wonderful thing
you just did for me.

20:21.073 --> 20:24.737
I can't believe this is coming out
of my mouth, but I love...

20:59.044 --> 21:01.569
So you got a tank, big whoop.
Want to fight about it?

21:22.398 --> 21:24.923
Well, I'm glad
that Superstore USA is gone.

21:25.034 --> 21:26.731
That place was nothing but trouble.

21:26.837 --> 21:28.202
And I think we learned something.

21:28.305 --> 21:31.797
Any problem caused by a tank
can be solved by a tank.

21:31.909 --> 21:34.503
Dad, you were about to say something
in the store.

21:34.611 --> 21:37.307
- No, I don't think so.
- No, I'm sure of it.

21:37.414 --> 21:40.007
<i>I don't know. Something about
Hardcastle and McCormick?</i>

21:40.117 --> 21:42.744
No, you were going to say you love me.

21:42.852 --> 21:45.378
You love me, and you know it.

21:45.489 --> 21:47.616
Hey, hey, mouth, young lady.

21:47.724 --> 21:50.055
Well, you think
you'll look for another job, Meg?

21:51.460 --> 21:52.791
Meg!

21:52.895 --> 21:54.158
Meg!

21:54.264 --> 21:55.458
Meg!

21:58.000 --> 21:59.297
Pardon me.

21:59.298 --> 23:00.298
Thank you for watching «Family Guy» on
www.FOX-fan.ru